{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_014ZxibDMGjLR4kgU8R1NExv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Written and committed **Q15: Time to first token — why matter for UX?**\n\nKey content in the note:\n\n- **Core distinction**: TTFT = network + prefill time only; the decode phase doesn't contribute. This is what most candidates miss.\n- **Why it matters for UX**: the \"blank screen\" metric — users tolerate long generation if they see tokens appearing within ~200–500 ms; perceived responsiveness ≠ total latency.\n- **4-lever mitigation stack** (in implementation-difficulty order):\n  1. **Prompt compression** (LLMLingua, selective context) — cuts prefill length, directly cuts TTFT\n  2. **Streaming** — only improves *perceived* TTFT, not actual prefill time\n  3. **Model tiering** (GPT-4o-mini, Llama 3 8B) — 2–3× faster prefill, tradeoff quality\n  4. **Semantic caching** — bypasses prefill entirely for repeated queries (<10 ms)\n- **Streaming-vs-post-processing conflict**: streaming is blocked when you need the full response for JSON parsing or NLI faithfulness checks — in that case optimise TTLT instead.\n- **Production numbers**: before/after table at 500K queries/day showing TTFT p50/p95 for different configurations.\n\n9 more plan items remain (Q16–Q23 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":68159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0b973e0-2886-41da-b937-aef012b8b390","uuid":"3b64fa13-f12c-4605-9edd-47f5dc8524be"}
